    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `telephoneDisplay` field so the API returns the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans, while `telephone` stays raw E.164.\n\nThree changes, following the existing patterns in this codebase:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `telephoneDisplay` read-only string property to the `Owner` response schema (alongside the other derived fields), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`.../rest/function/owner/TelephoneDisplay.java`** (new) \u2014 a helper (mirroring `OwnerLocality`/`OwnerIdentityKey`) that formats an E.164 number as `country code` + space + national digits grouped in threes: `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`. Country-code length is 1 for NANP (`+1`) and 2 otherwise (covers `+61`), consistent with `TelephoneE164`. Malformed/non-E.164 input is returned unchanged.\n\n3. **`.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired `telephoneDisplay` via a MapStruct `@Mapping(... expression = ...)`, exactly like `locality` and `identityKey`.\n\nThe new acceptance test (`coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay`) passes \u2014 `$.telephone` is `+61412345678` and `$.telephoneDisplay` is `+61 412 345 678` \u2014 and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
